From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec: restart both queues on flush

Seeking in mpv with hwdec=v4l2m2m-copy on the Retroid Pocket Nova
(Qualcomm iris, kernel 7.2.5) freezes the picture while the audio plays
on. Reproduced without a display: after a seek the decoder logs

  h264_v4l2m2m: VIDIOC_DECODER_CMD start error: 16
  h264_v4l2m2m: capture: driver decode error

twice, and the video position never moves again. With hwdec off the same
seeks are fine.

The flush that the v4l2-drmprime patch adds does STREAMOFF and STREAMON
on the OUTPUT (bitstream) queue only, then V4L2_DEC_CMD_START. That is
the seek the V4L2 stateful decoder interface describes. On iris the
START is refused with EBUSY (the driver allows it only while draining or
during a resolution change), and after the OUTPUT restart the decoder
returns two error frames and then nothing: it keeps the input buffers it
holds and never asks for more, so v4l2_receive_frame blocks in poll().

Restart the whole pipeline instead: STREAMOFF on both queues, mark the
buffers the driver handed back as available, STREAMON on the OUTPUT
queue, queue the free capture buffers and STREAMON there too, in the
order ff_v4l2_context_init used the first time. A capture buffer still
held by a frame comes back through v4l2_free_buffer when the frame is
released. GStreamer's v4l2 decoder flushes the same way. The DEC_CMD
START is dropped; a full restart makes it moot.

Applies on top of the v4l2-drmprime patch, which introduced the flush.
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c	2026-09-25 00:33:12
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c	2026-09-25 00:33:12
@@ -260,30 +260,58 @@
     V4L2m2mContext* s = priv->context;
     V4L2Context* output = &s->output;
     V4L2Context* capture = &s->capture;
+    int capture_was_on = capture->streamon;
     int ret, i;
 
-    struct v4l2_decoder_cmd cmd = {
-        .cmd = V4L2_DEC_CMD_START,
-        .flags = 0,
-    };
-
+    /* Stop both queues. STREAMOFF on the OUTPUT queue alone is what the
+     * V4L2 stateful decoder interface calls a seek, and it is all this
+     * did before. On Qualcomm's iris the decoder then hands back two
+     * frames flagged as errors and nothing more: it keeps the output
+     * buffers it holds and never asks for input again, so the caller sits
+     * in poll() and the picture stands still while the audio plays on.
+     * Stopping the CAPTURE queue too restarts the whole pipeline, which is
+     * what GStreamer's v4l2 decoder does on a flush. */
     ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(output, VIDIOC_STREAMOFF);
     if (ret < 0)
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_STREAMOFF %s error: %d\n", output->name, ret);
 
-    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(output, VIDIOC_STREAMON);
-    if (ret < 0)
-        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_STREAMON %s error: %d\n", output->name, ret);
+    if (capture_was_on) {
+        ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(capture, VIDIOC_STREAMOFF);
+        if (ret < 0)
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_STREAMOFF %s error: %d\n", capture->name, ret);
+    }
 
+    /* STREAMOFF returns every queued buffer; the bookkeeping follows. A
+     * capture buffer still held by a frame is not touched: it comes back
+     * through v4l2_free_buffer when the frame is released. */
     for (i = 0; i < output->num_buffers; i++) {
         if (output->buffers[i].status == V4L2BUF_IN_DRIVER)
             output->buffers[i].status = V4L2BUF_AVAILABLE;
     }
+    if (capture->buffers) {
+        for (i = 0; i < capture->num_buffers; i++) {
+            if (capture->buffers[i].status == V4L2BUF_IN_DRIVER)
+                capture->buffers[i].status = V4L2BUF_AVAILABLE;
+        }
+    }
 
-    ret = ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_DECODER_CMD, &cmd);
+    /* Start again in the order the decoder was started: input first, then
+     * the capture side with its free buffers queued, as ff_v4l2_context_init
+     * did the first time. */
+    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(output, VIDIOC_STREAMON);
     if (ret < 0)
-        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_DECODER_CMD start error: %d\n", errno);
+        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_STREAMON %s error: %d\n", output->name, ret);
 
+    if (capture_was_on) {
+        for (i = 0; i < capture->num_buffers; i++) {
+            if (capture->buffers[i].status == V4L2BUF_AVAILABLE)
+                ff_v4l2_buffer_enqueue(&capture->buffers[i]);
+        }
+        ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_status(capture, VIDIOC_STREAMON);
+        if (ret < 0)
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "VIDIOC_STREAMON %s error: %d\n", capture->name, ret);
+    }
+
     s->draining = 0;
     output->done = 0;
     capture->done = 0;
